==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bɹiː/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|iː|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|bre}}, {{m|enm|bregh}}, from {{inh|en|ang|brēġ||eyelid}} {{i|Anglian dialect}}. Compare West Saxon {{m|ang|brǣw}}, {{m|ang|brēaw}}, {{m|ang|brēaġ||eyelid}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*brēwō}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|wenkbrauw|(wenk)brauw}}, {{cog|de|Braue}}. Apparently related to {{m|en|brow}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|dialectal|Scotland}} The [[eyelid]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|dialectal|Scotland}} The [[eyebrow]].
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} The [[brow]]; [[forehead]].

===Etymology 2===
The word could be an immediate cognate of {{cog|de|Brühe||broth}}, from {{cog|gmh|brüeje}}, from the verb {{m|gmh|brüejen||to scald, boil}}, from {{cog|gem-pro|*brōjaną}}, whence modern {{cog|de|brühen}}, {{cog|nl|broeien}}, {{cog|gml|brȫjen}}. This is uncertain, however, since the verb is not attested in English nor in {{etyl|non|-}}. At any rate, eventually from the {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} root {{m|ine-pro|*bʰrewh₁-}}, whence also {{cog|en|broth}} and {{m|en|brew}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|outside|Scotland}} [[broth|Broth]].

===Anagrams===
* {{l|en|beer}}
* {{l|en|bere}}

